{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30233 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Angoroside-C may interact with SNU1, through a series of molecular targets that ultimately converge on the same downstream effect. Angoroside-C is implicated in the pathway leading to Caspase-5, which is a key regulator of apoptosis. Caspase-5 is then targeted by two different compounds—5-Oxobrucine and Lancifodilactone N—both of which also target SNU1. This indicates that Angoroside-C may exert its effects via a shared pathway, possibly by modulating Caspase-5 activity, which in turn influences SNU1. The consistent presence of Caspase-5 as a common target across all three paths supports a mechanistic link between Angoroside-C and SNU1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected biological roles of these molecules, suggesting a plausible, though not yet fully characterized, relationship.",
